diff --git a/PAYMENTS.md b/PAYMENTS.md
index ee24a69..608667d 100644
--- a/PAYMENTS.md
+++ b/PAYMENTS.md
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-# Payments, timeline and documents — v1.13.0
+# Payments, timeline and documents — v1.14.0
 
 See [the current user guide](USER_GUIDE.md) for Quick start, task guides, FAQ, closeout, backup and troubleshooting instructions. This replaces the old release-by-release instruction appendices.
 
@@ -30,3 +30,7 @@ The main Export & Share budget PDF follows the approved grey-shaded Top Sheet/de
 ## v1.13.0 vendor dashboards
 - Vendors have a visual directory and a per-vendor view for the selected budget. Link unassigned detail lines, schedule fixed dated amounts per line, record payments explicitly, and see daily unpaid totals in the vendor calendar. Advanced shared/percentage/milestone flows remain available.
 - Vendor agreements are stored locally with the reusable vendor, not in the budget document binder or ZIP. A single-budget backup includes agreement originals for referenced vendors; a workspace backup includes all vendor agreements. Originals are copied on restore. Each file may be up to 100 MB; there is no fixed number-of-agreements limit.
+
+## Crew, cast and visual timelines
+
+Crew and Cast are separate views of the shared local contact book. Choose all relevant categories when creating or editing a contact; an existing uncategorized contact remains under Vendors until categorized. Deal memos, W-9/W-2 files and other agreements stay local, with full originals in workspace backups and referenced-contact originals in single-budget backups. These backups are sensitive. The app does not process or file tax forms. Vendor logos are locally stored and backed up with contact information. Production phases and custom milestones are shown on a shared date axis; the main calendar scrolls through months without changing financial calculations.
diff --git a/USER_GUIDE.md b/USER_GUIDE.md
index 9a9c46e..237c433 100644
--- a/USER_GUIDE.md
+++ b/USER_GUIDE.md
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-# NO LONGER BUDGET — User guide (v1.13.0)
+# NO LONGER BUDGET — User guide (v1.14.0)
 
 Current workflow; release history lives in GitHub and the Build Log.
 
@@ -65,6 +65,10 @@ Click the **# heading → Renumber**. Accounts renumber by hundreds within the c
 
 ### Setup, globals and live expressions
 
+**Crew and Cast:** In Payments & Timeline, use the Crew and Cast tabs for individual contacts. Choose one or more categories when creating or editing a contact; existing contacts stay in Vendors until categorized. A contact shared across categories is one record, with one set of locally stored agreements. Add deal memos, W-9/W-2 files and other documents from the contact dashboard. The app does not process or file tax forms. Full backups include these sensitive files; protect backup copies.
+
+**Timeline:** Production phases and custom milestones appear visually on a shared date axis. The Calendar tab scrolls through months; its month selector controls the downloaded month.
+
 **Vendor dashboard:** Choose Setup → Vendors, add a vendor, and open its dashboard. Add signed agreements (100 MB per file), link unassigned detail lines, then schedule payments on each line. The dashboard shows expected final, net paid, scheduled unpaid, unscheduled amounts and a monthly calendar with daily due totals for this budget. Vendor agreements are reusable on this computer; lines and payment records are budget-specific.
 
 **Setup** opens Globals, Units, Fringes, Groups, Currency, Vendors, Payments & Timeline, Timeline & Funding and Documents. Close a manager/workspace with its × control. Vendors are a shared contact book; budget setup and payment records belong to the selected budget.
