-    "body": "<p><b>Vendor dashboard:</b> choose Setup → Vendors, add a vendor, then open its dashboard. Add as many signed agreements as needed (100 MB per file), choose Link budget lines and select unassigned detail lines. Each linked line can have one or more individually dated payments. The dashboard shows expected final, net paid, scheduled unpaid, unscheduled amounts and a monthly calendar with daily due totals for this budget. Agreements are shared with the reusable vendor on this computer; the budget lines and payment history are budget-specific.</p><p><b>Setup</b> opens Globals, Units, Fringes, Groups, Currency, Vendors, Payments &amp; Timeline, Timeline &amp; Funding and Documents. Close a manager/workspace with its × control. Vendors are a shared contact book; budget setup and payment records belong to the selected budget.</p><p>Setup → Globals stores named numbers, text or expressions referencing other globals, such as <code>Day Rate * 5</code>. Type a global name directly into Description, QTY, UNIT, X or RATE; autocomplete helps. There is no chain-link button. Leaving a field displays the resolved value; selecting it restores the expression. Updates propagate to references. Uses counts name occurrences in detail fields and other globals—not just distinct rows.</p>"
+    "body": "<p><b>Crew and Cast:</b> In Payments &amp; Timeline, use the Crew and Cast tabs for individual contacts. Choose one or more categories when creating or editing a contact; existing contacts stay in Vendors until categorized. A contact shared across categories is one record, with one set of locally stored agreements. Add deal memos, W-9/W-2 files and other documents from the contact dashboard. The app does not process or file tax forms. Full backups include these sensitive files; protect backup copies.</p><p><b>Timeline:</b> Production phases and custom milestones appear visually on a shared date axis. The Calendar tab scrolls through months; its month selector controls the downloaded month.</p><p><b>Vendor dashboard:</b> choose Setup → Vendors, add a vendor, then open its dashboard. Add as many signed agreements as needed (100 MB per file), choose Link budget lines and select unassigned detail lines. Each linked line can have one or more individually dated payments. The dashboard shows expected final, net paid, scheduled unpaid, unscheduled amounts and a monthly calendar with daily due totals for this budget. Agreements are shared with the reusable vendor on this computer; the budget lines and payment history are budget-specific.</p><p><b>Setup</b> opens Globals, Units, Fringes, Groups, Currency, Vendors, Payments &amp; Timeline, Timeline &amp; Funding and Documents. Close a manager/workspace with its × control. Vendors are a shared contact book; budget setup and payment records belong to the selected budget.</p><p>Setup → Globals stores named numbers, text or expressions referencing other globals, such as <code>Day Rate * 5</code>. Type a global name directly into Description, QTY, UNIT, X or RATE; autocomplete helps. There is no chain-link button. Leaving a field displays the resolved value; selecting it restores the expression. Updates propagate to references. Uses counts name occurrences in detail fields and other globals—not just distinct rows.</p>"
